  "title": "nginx: five memory-safety flaws, unauthenticated code execution demonstrated",
  "nicknames": ["NGINX2Root"],
  "summary": "Five nginx vulnerabilities in HTTP/2, HTTP/3, the resolver and the mail proxy, fixed in nginx 1.31.9 (mainline) and 1.30.7 (stable). Each needs a specific configuration. The finders demonstrated unauthenticated remote code execution in a research setting. NGINX Plus is affected too; the CNA records also list NGINX Plus R33 and earlier. CIRCL also describes a Linux SCTP privilege escalation without a CVE id; it is not part of this card.",
  "published_at": "2026-11-18T15:00:00Z",
  "updated_at": "2026-11-18T18:00:00Z",
  "severity": {
    "level": "critical",
    "note": "CNA score CVSS 4.0 9.2 CRITICAL for each of the five (CVSS 3.1 8.1 HIGH).",
    "sources": ["cve-2026-123007", "cve-2026-123633", "cve-2026-123634", "cve-2026-121810", "cve-2026-113425"]
  },
